QuietNote is derived from Scratch by Eric Li and contributors:
https://github.com/erictli/scratch
Audited upstream commit: 9126a5adf78abbabd111302ca0b659ca9278d43a

The upstream README declares the project MIT licensed. That checkout did not
contain a LICENSE file or a separate copyright notice. The original README is
preserved verbatim in docs/UPSTREAM-README.md. LICENSE supplies the standard MIT
text and explicit upstream attribution; it is not represented as a verbatim
license file recovered from upstream. Original source authorship is retained in
git history and Cargo metadata. Scratch is acknowledged as the upstream project,
not used as QuietNote product branding.

Third-party service logos in src/quietnote/brands/ come from the Iconify "logos"
set (CC0-1.0), vscode-icons (MIT, the Outlook mark) and Simple Icons (CC0-1.0,
the Google Docs mark). The trademarks belong to their owners and are shown only
to identify each service in Connections. Apple Calendar, Apple Reminders and
Things icons are not bundled; on macOS they are read from the apps installed on
the user's Mac.

The macOS and Windows builds bundle speech models that are downloaded at build
time by scripts/fetch-models.mjs and are not stored in this repository: OpenAI's
Whisper large-v3-turbo model (MIT, https://github.com/openai/whisper) in the
ggml format published with whisper.cpp (MIT, https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp),
and the Silero voice activity detector (MIT, https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad)
in the ggml format published by ggml-org. whisper.cpp is linked through whisper-rs.
